---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Sidekick: stay in the talk and meet the right people"
  description="Sidekick checks the room at an event and ranks who is worth meeting. You decide who to connect with, and nobody sees who you passed on."
>
  <header class="top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="/"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Sidekick</a>
      <nav aria-label="Main">
        <a href="#how">How it works</a>
        <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a href="#questions">Questions</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://sidekick.artifisi.com">Open the app</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">For people who go to events to meet people</p>
          <h1>Stay in the talk. Your sidekick works the room.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Check in to an event and Sidekick ranks the people there by what they are looking for and what they can offer.
            You swipe to connect or pass. When you both connect, you get each other's contact details and an opener for the break.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://sidekick.artifisi.com">Open Sidekick</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#how">See how it works</a>
          </div>
          <p class="status">Runs in the browser, no install needed. Still in pilot.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="phone" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="screen">
            <div class="screen-head"><span>Your sidekick</span><b>Demo event</b></div>
            <div class="deck-stack">
              <article class="person back">
                <div class="avatar">A</div>
                <h3>Amir</h3>
                <p class="role">Product lead, payments</p>
                <p class="fit">Wants to hire a designer. Can share notes on running a pilot.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="person top">
                <span class="stamp">CONNECT</span>
                <div class="avatar">D</div>
                <h3>Daniel</h3>
                <p class="role">CTO, logistics startup</p>
                <p class="fit">Can offer engineering help and mentorship. Looking for early customers.</p>
                <div class="tags"><span>Engineering</span><span>Mentorship</span><span>Logistics</span></div>
                <div class="swipe-row">
                  <span>Pass</span>
                  <span class="connect">Connect</span>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="problem band-oat" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
          <h2 id="problem-title">At an event you have to pick between the talk and the people you came to meet.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="reveal">
          <li><span class="n">1</span><p>Leave the talk to find one person, and miss the rest of the session.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">2</span><p>Stay in the talk, and leave with no introductions.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">3</span><p>Work the room with no way to tell who fits what you need.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="steps-head reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
          <h2 id="how-title">Three steps, and the room does the searching.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <article class="step reveal">
            <span class="num">1</span>
            <h3>Check in</h3>
            <p>Check in to the event, or to a place like a coworking space. Sidekick sends your sidekick to scout the room.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step reveal">
            <span class="num">2</span>
            <h3>Swipe on the people</h3>
            <p>Each card shows what someone is looking for and what they can offer. Read the sidekicks' conversation first, then connect or pass.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step reveal">
            <span class="num">3</span>
            <h3>Match and talk</h3>
            <p>When you both connect, you get each other's contact details and an opener for the break. Nobody sees a pass.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="talk band-pine" aria-labelledby="talk-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Before you swipe</p>
          <h2 id="talk-title">Read what the two sidekicks would say to each other.</h2>
          <p class="talk-note">
            The conversation is built from the two profiles only. It says nothing about who has swiped on whom,
            so it helps you decide without showing anyone's choices.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="chat reveal" role="group" aria-label="Example conversation from the demo event">
          <p class="chat-label">Example from the demo event</p>
          <div class="turn mine"><small>Your sidekick</small>I'm with Raja, a builder. Looking for funding.</div>
          <div class="turn"><small>Daniel's sidekick</small>I'm with Daniel, CTO at a logistics startup. Can offer engineering help and mentorship.</div>
          <div class="turn mine"><small>Your sidekick</small>Raja would value the conversation.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h2 id="privacy-title">Your choices stay with you.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="privacy-list reveal">
          <li><span><strong>Passes are never shown.</strong> No one can see who you passed on, or who passed on them.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Contact details come only after a match.</strong> A match needs both people to connect.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Profiles are only shown to their owner.</strong> Other people see the card for the event, not your account.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Blocks work both ways.</strong> Once you block someone, neither of you sees the other.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="questions" class="faq band-oat" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
          <h2 id="faq-title">What people ask first.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <details open>
            <summary>Do I need to sign in?</summary>
            <p>No. You can fill in a profile, check in and see your sidekick's picks as a guest. To connect with people you sign in with Google, and your guest details move across to your account.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Does it work on Android and on the web?</summary>
            <p>Yes. The same app runs in the browser at sidekick.artifisi.com, and there is also an Android app that uses the same account.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can the other person see that I passed?</summary>
            <p>No. A pass is private. Only a connection that both people make leads to a match.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Who can see my photo?</summary>
            <p>Photos are optional. They are checked to be a JPEG, PNG or WebP image of up to 2 MB. Other people in the same event see the photo on your card.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Has it been used at a real event?</summary>
            <p>Not yet. Sidekick is in pilot and has been tested on a demo event with sample people. Check-in does not verify where someone is yet, so anyone can check in from anywhere during the pilot.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final band-pine" aria-labelledby="final-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow reveal">Try it at your next event</p>
        <h2 id="final-title" class="reveal">Go to the talk. Let your sidekick find the people.</h2>
        <div class="actions reveal">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://sidekick.artifisi.com">Open Sidekick</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#how">How it works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span>Sidekick, made by Artifisi Sdn Bhd.</span>
      <a href="https://sidekick.artifisi.com">sidekick.artifisi.com</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Base>
